[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943815785","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107134#issuecomment-2943815785","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107134","id":2943815785,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vdxBp","user":{"login":"retrotails","id":10767978,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzY3OTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10767978?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails","html_url":"https://github.com/retrotails","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T11:29:40Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T11:29:40Z","body":"so with the knowledge it's caused by 1e20 being different from Math::INF somehow, I've done some more digging.\nI've traced this specific issue to these lines in voxelizer.cpp:930\n```cpp\n\tr_image.resize(float_count);\n\t{\n\t\tuint8_t *w = r_image.ptrw();\n\t\tfor (uint32_t i = 0; i < float_count; i++) {\n\t\t\tuint32_t d = uint32_t(Math::sqrt(work_memory[i]));\n\t\t\tif (d == 0) {\n\t\t\t\tw[i] = 0;\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tw[i] = MIN(d, 254u) + 1;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n```\nthis hack for example fixes this issue\n```diff\n \t\tuint8_t *w = r_image.ptrw();\n \t\tfor (uint32_t i = 0; i < float_count; i++) {\n+\t\t\tif (work_memory[i] == Math::INF) { work_memory[i] = 1e20; }\n \t\t\tuint32_t d = uint32_t(Math::sqrt(work_memory[i]));\n \t\t\tif (d == 0) {\n```\nthe difference between Math::INF and 1e20 here is:\n`uint32_t( Math::sqrt( Math::INF ) )` == `0`\nwheras:\n`uint32_t( Math::sqrt( float( 1e20 ) ) )` == `1410065408`\nI guess it's a c++ quirk that casting infinity to uint32_t produces 0; I would have expected either an error or INT_MAX.\n\n\nI think the solution is to revert all the changes from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105249 where Math::INF was replacing a non-infinite value. I see a very similar case in `core/math/geometry_3d.cpp` for example.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943815785/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943824480","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107134#issuecomment-2943824480","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107134","id":2943824480,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vdzJg","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T11:33:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T11:33:05Z","body":"> I think the solution is to revert all the changes from [#105249](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105249) where Math::INF was replacing a non-infinite value. I see a very similar case in `core/math/geometry_3d.cpp` for example.\n\nYeah I think this was a review oversight but such a refactoring PR should never have included actual logic changes. These should be reverted. CC @Repiteo @Ivorforce ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943824480/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2943863579","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107134#issuecomment-2943863579","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107134","id":2943863579,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vd8sb","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url"